        up-front, then wraps the whole batch in one SQLite
        `Connection::transaction()` so any per-entry failure rolls back the
        full batch.
      - Registered the new command in `lib.rs` behind the existing `crypto`
        feature (matches the other `db_*` commands).
      - Rewired `createTauriRepo.transaction(fn)` to buffer puts and deletes
        inside the callback and dispatch them as ONE `db_put_batch` call.
        A throw from `fn` short-circuits before any IPC, so the database is
        untouched. Reads inside the callback observe the pre-tx state.
      - Refactored `enqueueOutboxEntry` to take a single shared repo: the
        entity row and the outbox row now live in the same namespace; the
        outbox row's id uses the reserved `__outbox__<mutationId>` prefix.
        `nextOutboxBatch` filters on that prefix to extract outbox rows
        from a heterogeneous namespace. Passing two different repos now
        throws `E3009` because separate namespaces cannot commit atomically.
      - Updated `docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md` §6.1 with the
        `db_put_batch` row and the new buffered-batch atomicity model.
      - Updated `packages/core-data-sqlite-driver/docs/dev_log.md` and
        `packages/single-table-todos-e2e/docs/dev_log.md` to retract the
        misleading "same-transaction rollback is proved" phrasing and
        record the P0 fix with the real per-driver atomicity story.
    
    Scope:
      - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/commands/database.rs (+ 4 cargo tests)
      - apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/lib.rs (command registration)
      - packages/core-data/src/sync-outbox.ts (single-repo refactor)
      - packages/core-data/src/tauri-sqlite.ts (buffered transaction)
      - packages/core-data/src/index.ts (export OUTBOX_ID_PREFIX, helpers)
      - packages/core-data/tests/sync-outbox.test.ts (9 cases incl.
        real-SQLite sabotage)
      - packages/core-data/tests/tauri-sqlite.test.ts (3 new cases for
        buffered transaction + Rust-side rollback)
      - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md §6.1
      - packages/core-data-sqlite-driver/docs/dev_log.md
      - packages/single-table-todos-e2e/docs/dev_log.md
    
    Risk:
      - Behavioural change for callers using `createTauriRepo.transaction()`:
        reads inside the callback now observe the pre-transaction state
        (no read-after-write within a tx). Documented in the factory's doc
        comment. No production caller exercises read-after-write inside a
        transaction today.
      - `EnqueueOutboxInput` keeps `outboxRepo` as an optional field for
        backwards source compatibility but enforces at runtime that it
        matches `entityRepo`. The only callers in-tree are tests, which
        were migrated.
      - No new dependencies; reuses bundled-sqlcipher rusqlite already
        behind the `crypto` feature.
    
    Docs:
      - docs/contracts/tauri-commands-v0.md §6.1 — `db_put_batch` row.
      - packages/core-data-sqlite-driver/docs/dev_log.md — Work Log entry +
        deferred-item retraction.
      - packages/single-table-todos-e2e/docs/dev_log.md — Phase 1 rewrite,
        verification notes, Work Log entry.
    
    Tests:
      - `cargo check` — PASS
      - `cargo check --features crypto` — PASS
      - `cargo test --features crypto database::` — 13/13 PASS
        (4 new: batch atomic commit, invalid-op rollback, runtime-error
        rollback, mixed put/delete order)
      - `pnpm --filter @repo/core-data test` — 66/66 PASS
        (sync-outbox now exercises in-memory + real-SQLite sabotage,
        tauri-sqlite proves buffered batch + Rust-side rollback)
      - `pnpm --filter @repo/core-data check-types` — PASS
      - `pnpm --filter desktop build` — PASS
    
